5 Oct, RHCSA Exam Question #1
Network Foundation and Persistent Identity
Purpose: To make the IP static
Things to do: Change the hostname, make the ip persistent

Steps:
`nmtui`, then select "edit connection", in the edit option enX0 option change ipv4 configuration to Manual, then press tab and add the address with the mask. (192.168.1.97/24)
Add the gateway address
Add the DNS server 8.8.8.8, then save and exit
nmcli connection reload
nmcli connection up enX0
nmcli connection show


NOTE: If nmcli or nmtui command isn't working in the exam, try systemctl status NetworkManager, then systemctl restart NetworkManager

Just like servers have NIC cards that are physical, VMs in that server have adapters that allocate Virtual CPU, RAM and storage to those VMs. By deactivating enX0, you turn off the adapter which causes the VM to just shut off. To turn it back on you have to go to Xen, and type nmcli connecton up enX0

RS232 = 8 pin D connection